CLASS:: KSTrace
summary:: An oscTap that records every message EventScheduler sends
categories:: Scheduling
related:: Classes/EventScheduler

DESCRIPTION::
Set as link::Classes/EventScheduler#-oscTap::, it keeps one record per OSC message (one per message of a bundle) plus the player's code::#:: lifecycle lines, and writes them as JSONL in the code::klotho-supersonic-trace/1:: format: code::{"t": tag - playStart | null, "addr", "args", "sent"}::, with code::late:: and code::purged:: flags. code::stop:: marks the bundles already handed to scsynth for later instants as purged. Such a trace is what the parity harness compares with the SuperSonic oracle's.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
ARGUMENT:: path
Where code::write:: puts the file.
ARGUMENT:: header
A Dictionary or Event written as the first line, code::{"header": {...}}::. Give it code::firstPrivateAudioBus::.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: tap
The hook EventScheduler calls.

METHOD:: markPurgedAfter
METHOD:: records
METHOD:: lines
METHOD:: write
